580
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:48,840
aren't the same thing.

581
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:50,200
With an enemy,

582
00:19:50,200 --> 00:19:51,160
there's usually a winner and a loser.

583
00:19:51,160 --> 00:19:52,400
(Expert Sami)
But an opponent can sometimes

584
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:54,160
make you think more deeply

585
00:19:54,160 --> 00:19:55,800
about your own role

586
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:57,520
and where you stand.

587
00:19:57,520 --> 00:19:59,000
So their fair competition

588
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,400
and interactions here

589
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:01,980
(Fair love. Respect either way)
are pretty clear.

590
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:02,760
Fiona, in your everyday life,

591
00:20:02,760 --> 00:20:05,440
are you the one who gives advice,

592
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:06,840
or the one who needs friends

593
00:20:06,840 --> 00:20:08,640
to give you advice?

594
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:09,720
I...

595
00:20:09,720 --> 00:20:11,040
(I don't give specific advice)
I don't give them advice.

596
00:20:11,040 --> 00:20:12,560
When I do give advice,

597
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:13,360
I'm not looking at it

598
00:20:13,360 --> 00:20:14,680
from a girl's perspective,

599
00:20:14,680 --> 00:20:15,440
nor am I looking at it

600
00:20:15,440 --> 00:20:16,280
from a guy's perspective.

601
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:17,320
I look at it

602
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:18,040
from the perspective

603
00:20:18,040 --> 00:20:19,280
of what's best

604
00:20:19,280 --> 00:20:20,480
for the relationship.

605
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:21,560
I will

606
00:20:21,560 --> 00:20:22,120
look at

607
00:20:22,120 --> 00:20:23,400
what their problem is

608
00:20:23,400 --> 00:20:24,360
and then help him (her)

609
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:27,360
find the happiest version
of himself (herself).

610
00:20:27,620 --> 00:20:28,340
(There's something to that)

611
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:29,000
You...

612
00:20:29,320 --> 00:20:30,800
You're like a therapist.

613
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:32,160
(Healing hearts)
I feel healed.

614
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:34,640
I think when you're in love,

615
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:36,480
you don't just love that person.

616
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:37,760
Sometimes,

617
00:20:37,760 --> 00:20:39,320
(Seeing yourself through them)
you see a part

618
00:20:39,320 --> 00:20:40,240
of yourself in them.

619
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:41,280
(Absolutely agree)
Exactly.

620
00:20:41,280 --> 00:20:42,480
That's so true.

621
00:20:43,080 --> 00:20:44,240
That is so true.

622
00:20:44,240 --> 00:20:45,120
Then you'll always

623
00:20:45,120 --> 00:20:45,720
stay by his (her) side,

624
00:20:45,720 --> 00:20:46,080
but deep down,

625
00:20:46,080 --> 00:20:47,320
you don't love him (her) that much.

626
00:20:47,320 --> 00:20:48,280
I don't think he (she)

627
00:20:48,280 --> 00:20:49,120
wants you to be

628
00:20:49,120 --> 00:20:49,920
that kind of person either.

629
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:53,160
So there's no trick.

630
00:20:53,160 --> 00:20:55,000
No move can be the best move.

631
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:56,120
Just look at JinZhao.

632
00:20:57,100 --> 00:20:58,460
(Just look at JinZhao couple)

633
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:00,040
Look at you.

634
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:02,600
Actually,

635
00:21:02,600 --> 00:21:03,440
Sun Bohan and Zhao Xilun

636
00:21:03,440 --> 00:21:04,160
are the same.

637
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:04,554
For example,

638
00:21:04,554 --> 00:21:05,540
even though their relationship

639
00:21:05,540 --> 00:21:06,600
hasn't even started yet,

640
00:21:06,600 --> 00:21:07,080
look at them.

641
00:21:07,080 --> 00:21:07,880
The way

642
00:21:07,880 --> 00:21:08,600
they talk about it.

643
00:21:08,600 --> 00:21:09,760
Maybe I know I'm lacking

644
00:21:09,760 --> 00:21:11,120
a little courage right now.

645
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:12,520
If he can

646
00:21:12,520 --> 00:21:13,400
understand all this

647
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:15,160
by the end of tonight,

648
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:16,120
that would be perfect.

649
00:21:16,120 --> 00:21:18,160
Right.
Knowing isn't enough. You have to act.

650
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:20,640
(The advice we give)
I think every time we advise someone,

651
00:21:20,640 --> 00:21:22,680
(is often meant for us too)
we've told ourselves the same thing.

652
00:21:22,680 --> 00:21:23,080
Right.

653
00:21:23,340 --> 00:21:24,340
(Agreed)

654
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:25,480
Right.

655
00:21:28,100 --> 00:21:32,580
(Cao Yiheng and Cui Kaiyi
return to the Signal House)

656
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:33,800
That's so pretty.

657
00:21:35,120 --> 00:21:35,640
Let's go.

658
00:21:36,440 --> 00:21:37,080
Go.

659
00:21:37,080 --> 00:21:37,440
Here.

660
00:21:37,440 --> 00:21:38,040
After you.

661
00:21:39,880 --> 00:21:41,200
The romantic "couple" is back.

662
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:43,720
Someone's chatting.

663
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:48,480
Let's hear the gossip

664
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:49,320
I'm loving this.

665
00:21:49,840 --> 00:21:50,760
Hello.

666
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:54,320
So romantic.

667
00:21:55,520 --> 00:21:57,280
Everything just got brighter.

668
00:21:58,680 --> 00:22:00,040
Keep going.

669
00:22:00,040 --> 00:22:00,720
We won't interrupt.

670
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:01,840
Bye bye.

671
00:22:02,240 --> 00:22:03,560
Your outfits match so well today.

672
00:22:03,560 --> 00:22:05,120
You two both look so good.

673
00:22:08,040 --> 00:22:08,280
Go.

674
00:22:09,720 --> 00:22:10,200
Let's go.

675
00:22:10,200 --> 00:22:10,520
Careful.

676
00:22:10,520 --> 00:22:11,800
I walked onto the grass.

677
00:22:12,560 --> 00:22:14,000
I was too busy watching them.

678
00:22:16,200 --> 00:22:18,160
She's so cute.

679
00:22:18,160 --> 00:22:19,200
Cui Kaiyi is hilarious.

680
00:22:20,080 --> 00:22:21,040
This lamp.

681
00:22:21,040 --> 00:22:22,000
It's so pretty.

682
00:22:23,560 --> 00:22:24,560
I like flowers too.

683
00:22:27,480 --> 00:22:28,240
Hello.

684
00:22:28,240 --> 00:22:30,360
Hi.

685
00:22:30,840 --> 00:22:32,560
What time did you guys get back?

686
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:35,720
We got back around eleven too.

687
00:22:35,720 --> 00:22:36,720
You just got back too.

688
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:37,120
Yeah.

689
00:22:37,120 --> 00:22:38,320
Go upstairs and change your shoes.

690
00:22:38,320 --> 00:22:39,440
I'll go up first.

691
00:22:39,440 --> 00:22:40,800
I totally forgot.

692
00:22:42,160 --> 00:22:43,680
I'll go up first
and come back down later.

693
00:22:49,120 --> 00:22:50,280
They match so well.

694
00:22:55,060 --> 00:22:56,540
(They both placed theirs by the bed)

695
00:22:56,560 --> 00:22:57,400
They really click.

696
00:22:58,080 --> 00:22:59,080
I'm going to the bathroom.

697
00:23:03,520 --> 00:23:04,680
I didn't sleep well last night.

698
00:23:04,680 --> 00:23:05,840
At least I can get
some good sleep tonight.

699
00:23:05,840 --> 00:23:06,800
Okay.

700
00:23:13,640 --> 00:23:14,640
What's wrong?

701
00:23:14,640 --> 00:23:15,600
Back to the room.

702
00:23:15,600 --> 00:23:16,720
Where did you just go?

703
00:23:17,080 --> 00:23:19,600
I went to ask someone out.

704
00:23:21,880 --> 00:23:23,080
The three of them are here.

705
00:23:23,080 --> 00:23:23,920
One bedroom.

706
00:23:23,920 --> 00:23:25,000
All like the same person.

707
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:26,320
How can they possibly sleep at night?

708
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:28,680
I don't know why.

709
00:23:28,680 --> 00:23:29,720
I just couldn't sleep peacefully.

710
00:23:29,720 --> 00:23:30,480
Yeah.

711
00:23:31,080 --> 00:23:32,120
Stargazing date.

712
00:23:32,120 --> 00:23:32,600
Yeah.

713
00:23:36,160 --> 00:23:37,320
I pressed that button.

714
00:23:38,080 --> 00:23:39,080
Then the light came on.

715
00:23:41,320 --> 00:23:43,760
Some are happy, some are worried.

716
00:23:44,920 --> 00:23:45,680
So basically,

717
00:23:45,680 --> 00:23:47,760
you used the Master Kong Jasmine Coin.

718
00:23:47,760 --> 00:23:48,600
I just used one.

719
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:50,880
I figured
it's been sitting there for days,

720
00:23:50,880 --> 00:23:52,120
and no one had used it.

721
00:23:52,120 --> 00:23:54,280
The way he said that
sounded pretty smug, huh?

722
00:23:55,240 --> 00:23:56,320
I figured
it's been sitting there for days,

723
00:23:56,320 --> 00:23:57,360
and no one had used it.

724
00:23:57,630 --> 00:23:59,120
(Asking)
Why weren't you in the stargazing room?

725
00:23:59,120 --> 00:24:00,200
Why were you outside?

726
00:24:00,200 --> 00:24:01,520
Maybe you have to book it in advance?

727
00:24:02,080 --> 00:24:03,590
(Follow-up question)
What's the process?

728
00:24:03,680 --> 00:24:06,000
There's actually one on the left
and one on the right.

729
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:06,640
So once you press them,

730
00:24:06,640 --> 00:24:08,240
something pops up right away?

731
00:24:11,340 --> 00:24:12,980
(Slowly rising)

732
00:24:15,480 --> 00:24:17,160
How do you choose then?

733
00:24:17,160 --> 00:24:18,280
Do you just say who you want to choose?

734
00:24:18,280 --> 00:24:19,000
Or...

735
00:24:19,240 --> 00:24:19,920
No.

736
00:24:20,760 --> 00:24:22,760
Because I didn't really

737
00:24:22,760 --> 00:24:23,720
understand the rules.

738
00:24:24,240 --> 00:24:25,960
You can actually go find her

739
00:24:25,960 --> 00:24:27,920
and give her that thing.

740
00:24:27,980 --> 00:24:29,600
(I see)

741
00:24:29,600 --> 00:24:31,160
We can only use it once a week.

742
00:24:31,160 --> 00:24:32,440
Is it within seven days,

743
00:24:32,440 --> 00:24:33,680
or is it based on...

744
00:24:33,680 --> 00:24:36,800
I think the once-a-week one
is the city date.

745
00:24:37,640 --> 00:24:39,040
But the stargazing room

746
00:24:39,040 --> 00:24:40,440
should be available every day.

747
00:24:42,320 --> 00:24:43,840
I have to get up early tomorrow.

748
00:24:43,840 --> 00:24:45,240
(Moving to a single room)
I'll sleep in that room tonight.

749
00:24:45,240 --> 00:24:46,120
Okay.

750
00:24:46,120 --> 00:24:48,040
Because I have something very important

751
00:24:48,920 --> 00:24:49,440
tomorrow.

752
00:24:49,440 --> 00:24:50,200
Yeah.

753
00:24:51,680 --> 00:24:52,240
Okay.

754
00:24:54,840 --> 00:24:56,280
Look, he doesn't dare sleep
in this room anymore.

755
00:24:58,440 --> 00:25:00,440
He's probably afraid
they'll keep an eye on him.

756
00:25:05,220 --> 00:25:06,860
(Well?)

757
00:25:08,080 --> 00:25:09,240
These two.

758
00:25:09,240 --> 00:25:10,640
They're about to get started.
The besties.

759
00:25:11,160 --> 00:25:11,920
How was your...

760
00:25:11,920 --> 00:25:13,740
(Stargazing card)

761
00:25:15,400 --> 00:25:16,000
Chen Hewen?

762
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:17,160
Yeah.

763
00:25:17,160 --> 00:25:18,320
So what happened yesterday?

764
00:25:18,740 --> 00:25:20,140
(Curious)
Yesterday,

765
00:25:20,800 --> 00:25:23,280
Liang Xiaoyu texted Chen Hewen.

766
00:25:25,120 --> 00:25:26,280
They cleared up the misunderstanding.

767
00:25:28,960 --> 00:25:30,320
I'm mad.

768
00:25:30,480 --> 00:25:32,040
What kind of guy is he?

769
00:25:32,040 --> 00:25:33,640
Men

770
00:25:33,640 --> 00:25:34,640
are like clothes.

771
00:25:36,400 --> 00:25:38,320
So cute.

772
00:25:38,320 --> 00:25:40,360
Cui Kaiyi is so cute.

773
00:25:42,880 --> 00:25:44,480
I just forgive him a little.

774
00:25:45,280 --> 00:25:46,800
So we misunderstood him yesterday.

775
00:25:46,800 --> 00:25:47,640
We misunderstood him.

776
00:25:47,640 --> 00:25:49,360
And we spent all that time analyzing it.

777
00:25:50,040 --> 00:25:51,640
Who would've thought it'd be this?

778
00:25:52,120 --> 00:25:52,920
She's so happy.

779
00:25:52,920 --> 00:25:54,360
Happy. She's genuinely happy.

780
00:25:54,360 --> 00:25:55,920
I'm kneeling again.

781
00:25:55,920 --> 00:25:58,160
You're completely different
from yesterday.

782
00:25:58,160 --> 00:25:59,400
Yesterday,
as soon as you came in, you were like,

783
00:26:01,600 --> 00:26:02,920
"What does he mean?"

784
00:26:04,960 --> 00:26:06,640
"I'm really mad."

785
00:26:06,640 --> 00:26:08,520
And today, you came in and just knelt.

786
00:26:08,520 --> 00:26:08,960
Knelt.

787
00:26:09,880 --> 00:26:11,000
Then you started laughing.

788
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:12,320
I give up.

789
00:26:13,040 --> 00:26:13,640
No.

790
00:26:14,120 --> 00:26:15,000
I should calm down a little.

791
00:26:16,880 --> 00:26:17,800
Stay calm.

792
00:26:17,800 --> 00:26:18,860
(Self-soothing)

793
00:26:19,120 --> 00:26:20,040
Stay calm.

794
00:26:20,840 --> 00:26:23,600
I'm actually not bothered at all.

795
00:26:23,600 --> 00:26:24,400
You know?

796
00:26:24,700 --> 00:26:25,860
(As if I'd believe you)

797
00:26:26,800 --> 00:26:29,120
What?

798
00:26:31,500 --> 00:26:32,460
(Gets up)

799
00:26:32,880 --> 00:26:33,840
What's wrong?
Is there a bug?

800
00:26:33,840 --> 00:26:34,880
No, I was checking myself out.

801
00:26:36,280 --> 00:26:37,680
Why am I blushing?

802
00:26:38,240 --> 00:26:38,880
Feeling pretty good, huh?

803
00:26:38,880 --> 00:26:40,600
Wonder if it's

804
00:26:40,600 --> 00:26:41,800
The Courageous

805
00:26:41,800 --> 00:26:43,640
or the stargazing card that did it.

806
00:26:46,760 --> 00:26:47,880
She's a smart one.

807
00:26:49,160 --> 00:26:51,200
Please. You made me blush.

808
00:26:51,200 --> 00:26:51,960
I did?

809
00:26:52,600 --> 00:26:53,320
Yeah.

810
00:26:53,320 --> 00:26:54,520
I blush every time I see you.

811
00:26:55,400 --> 00:26:56,520
Okay, I'll take your word for it.

812
00:26:57,240 --> 00:26:59,400
Oh, so that's what happened.

813
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:02,000
I kind of misunderstood him yesterday.

814
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:03,240
I feel bad.

815
00:27:03,240 --> 00:27:04,880
I don't feel bad.

816
00:27:04,880 --> 00:27:05,880
I do.

817
00:27:06,440 --> 00:27:07,680
You sure don't.

818
00:27:08,240 --> 00:27:09,600
These two are hilarious.

819
00:27:09,600 --> 00:27:10,800
I feel bad.

820
00:27:10,960 --> 00:27:12,120
This is too funny.

821
00:27:12,480 --> 00:27:13,640
She had him all wrong.

822
00:27:13,680 --> 00:27:15,600
Cui Kaiyi is seriously the best friend ever.

823
00:27:15,600 --> 00:27:16,480
Absolutely.

824
00:27:17,720 --> 00:27:18,960
I just remembered one I can play.

825
00:27:18,960 --> 00:27:19,600
Let me try it again.

826
00:27:19,600 --> 00:27:20,160
Okay.

827
00:27:21,560 --> 00:27:23,040
This place is so artsy.

828
00:27:27,760 --> 00:27:29,200
Wait, don't play yet.

829
00:27:30,160 --> 00:27:32,160
I wanna hear about your date today.

830
00:27:35,120 --> 00:27:36,320
Well...

831
00:27:36,320 --> 00:27:38,760
The scenery was actually really nice.

832
00:27:38,760 --> 00:27:39,720
And the guy was great.

833
00:27:39,720 --> 00:27:41,920
But Beijing traffic was awful,

834
00:27:41,920 --> 00:27:43,080
so I got a little

835
00:27:43,080 --> 00:27:44,120
carsick.

836
00:27:46,020 --> 00:27:47,560
(Laughs)
I mean...

837
00:27:47,560 --> 00:27:48,800
You went at the worst time

838
00:27:48,800 --> 00:27:50,560
for traffic in Beijing, right?

839
00:27:52,920 --> 00:27:54,560
Mine was pretty funny too.

840
00:27:54,560 --> 00:27:55,520
Our boat ride

841
00:27:55,520 --> 00:27:57,240
wasn't quite what I expected either.

842
00:27:57,240 --> 00:27:58,600
It was a kayak, so we had

843
00:27:58,600 --> 00:28:00,320
to face each other and paddle like this.

844
00:28:00,320 --> 00:28:01,800
And the water kept splashing us.

845
00:28:04,920 --> 00:28:05,760
The funniest part is,

846
00:28:05,760 --> 00:28:06,760
before I came here,

847
00:28:06,760 --> 00:28:08,080
I said I wasn't into looks.

848
00:28:08,080 --> 00:28:09,320
Then I got here
and completely proved myself wrong.

849
00:28:09,320 --> 00:28:10,440
I said I didn't care

850
00:28:10,440 --> 00:28:12,480
what someone looked like,

851
00:28:12,480 --> 00:28:14,640
and then I saw him
and completely folded.

852
00:28:15,480 --> 00:28:16,320
Love at first sight.

853
00:28:16,320 --> 00:28:17,360
She just loved his face.

854
00:28:18,120 --> 00:28:19,880
I have a question.

855
00:28:21,120 --> 00:28:23,240
Rank the guys by how handsome they are.

856
00:28:23,240 --> 00:28:23,840
Sure.

857
00:28:23,840 --> 00:28:25,400
Let's hear it.

858
00:28:25,400 --> 00:28:26,320
This'll be fun.

859
00:28:26,320 --> 00:28:27,160
Come on.

860
00:28:27,160 --> 00:28:30,240
Honestly, I think Zhao Xilun is the hottest.

861
00:28:30,240 --> 00:28:32,000
(Zhao Xilun is the hottest)
And then...

862
00:28:32,000 --> 00:28:33,920
Let me think about all the guys.

863
00:28:34,320 --> 00:28:34,760
I miss

864
00:28:34,760 --> 00:28:35,720
our time at the house.

865
00:28:36,240 --> 00:28:37,160
Did you rank us back then?

866
00:28:37,160 --> 00:28:37,760
No.

